==English==
{{wp}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|dem||nonstandard}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:þem|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|þem}}, from {{der|en|non|þeim}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|en|stressed}} {{enPR|''th''ĕm}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈðɛm/}}
** {{IPA|en|[ˈðɪm]|a=pen-pin merger}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-them.ogg|a=US}}
** {{IPA|en|[ˈðʌm]|a=nonstandard}}
** {{rhymes|en|ɛm|s=1}}
* {{q|unstressed}} {{enPR|''th''əm}}, {{IPA|en|/ðəm/}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-them-unstressed.ogg|a=US,unstressed|text=see them}}
* {{hyph|en|them}}

===Pronoun===
{{en-pron|desc=third-person, personal pronoun|objective case of|they}}

# {{lb|en|in the plural}} Those ones.
## {{n-g|Used as the direct object of a verb.}}
##: {{ux|en|She treated '''them''' for a cold.}}
##* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Amy Harmon|title=Which Box Do You Check? Some States Are Offering a Nonbinary Option|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/29/us/nonbinary-drivers-licenses.html|date=2019-05-29|passage=Proponents of adding a gender-neutral option to state identification documents say it would remove a form of discrimination against nonbinary people by providing '''them''' with the means to carry identification that matches their identity.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190608042105/https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/29/us/nonbinary-drivers-licenses.html}}
## {{n-g|Used as the indirect object of a verb.}}
##: {{ux|en|She wrote '''them''' a letter.}}
## {{n-g|Used as the object of a preposition.}}
##: {{ux|en|Give it to '''them'''.}}
## {{lb|en|nonstandard|or|colloquial|uncommon}} {{non-gloss|As a grammatical subject or object when joined with a conjunction.}}
##: {{ux|en|[...] and now '''them''' and the Goo Goo Dolls are playing together.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2006-09-27|author=David Ress|title=Governor Edward Coles and the Vote to Forbid Slavery in Illinois, 1823-1824|publisher=McFarland|isbn=9780786426393|page=64
|text={{...}}Illinois, told Christina Holmes Tillson (just arrived from Connecticut herself) : “I am getting skeery about them 'ere Yankees. There is such a power of them coming in that '''them''' and the Injuns will squatch out [everyone else].}}
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2021-06-10|author=Yvonne Bailey-Smith|title=The Day I Fell Off My Island|publisher=Myriad Editions|isbn=9781912408962
|text='''Them''' and the boys went to live with Auntie Madge and Uncle Herbie when Miss Violet died.}}
## {{non-gloss|Used in isolation or apposition, or}} {{lb|en|sometimes|proscribed}} {{non-gloss|as the [[complement]] of the [[copula]] (''[[be]]'').}}
##: {{ux|en|Who was there? &mdash;'''Them'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|Who did this? &mdash;'''Them'''. They did it. (or:) It was '''them'''. They did it.)}}
##: {{ux|en|Who did that? &mdash;(It was) not '''them''': I was watching them the whole time.}}
# {{lb|en|in the singular|occasionally|proscribed}} A single person, previously mentioned, whose [[gender]] is unknown, irrelevant, or {{lb|en|since 21st c.}} [[non-binary]].
## {{n-g|Used as the direct object of a verb.}}
##: {{ux|en|If a student has an inappropriate question, whatever you do, do not berate '''them'''.}}
##* {{RQ:KJV|Deuteronomy|17|2|5|passage=If there be found among you, within any of thy gates which the {{smallcaps|Lord}} thy God giveth thee, man or woman, that hath wrought wickedness in the sight of the {{smallcaps|Lord}} thy God, {{...}} [t]hen shalt thou bring forth that man or that woman, which have committed that wicked thing, unto thy gates, even that man or that woman, and shalt stone '''them''' with stones, till they die.}}
## {{n-g|Used as the indirect object of a verb.}}
##: {{ux|en|If one of my patients calls, please bring '''them''' their dinner.}}
## {{n-g|Used as the object of a preposition.}}
##: {{ux|en|If someone comes and asks for the ticket, just give it to '''them'''.}}
## {{lb|en|nonstandard|or|colloquial|uncommon}} {{non-gloss|As a grammatical subject or object when joined with a conjunction.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1969|author=United States. National Labor Relations Board|title=Decisions and Orders of the National Labor Relations Board|page=82
|text="{{...}} he said that everybody was being watched, and if they seen anybody giving Union cards to anybody on Company property, that '''them''' and the person receiving the card, they would both be fired.}}
## {{non-gloss|Used in isolation or apposition, or}} {{lb|en|sometimes|proscribed}} {{non-gloss|as the [[complement]] of the [[copula]] (''[[be]]'').}}
##: {{ux|en|Who was there? &mdash;'''Them'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|Who did this? &mdash;'''Them'''. They did it. (or:) It was '''them'''. They did it.)}}
##: {{ux|en|Who did that? &mdash;(It was) not '''them''': I was watching them the whole time.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|_|set phrases|dialectal|or|nonstandard}} [[they|They]]; [[those]].
#: {{ux|en|I know it seems unfair, but '''them'''{{'}}s the rules.}}
#: {{coi|en|[[them's the breaks|'''Them'''{{'}}s the breaks.]]}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Luke|1|50|51|passage=And his mercy is on '''them''' that feare him, from generation to generation. Hee hath shewed strength with his arme, he hath scattered the proud, in the imagination of their hearts.}}

